<exercises xml:id="ex-IncreasingDecreasing">
    <exercise>
        <p>
            Explain what a critical number of <m>f(x)</m> is. What are the things we're looking for?
        </p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                For the following functions, find the critical numbers and explain each one. Is it one where the derivative is 0, or one where the derivative doesn't exist? Feel free to confirm these by graphing the function!
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = x^2+5x-4</m> on <m>[-4,2]</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = 2x+5</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = 2x+5 </mrow>
                        <mrow>x \amp = -\frac{5}{2}</mrow>
                    </md>
                    The critical numbers are <m>4</m> (where <m>f'</m> doesn't exist), <m>-\frac{5}{2}</m> (where the derivative is 0), and <m>2</m> (where the derivative doesn't exist). 
                </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \sqrt[3]{x+4}</m> on <m>[-6,-2]</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = \frac{1}{3(x+4)^{2/3}} </mrow>
                    </md>
                    At <m>-6</m>, <m>-4</m> and <m>-2</m> we can see that <m>f'</m> doesn't exist. Since these are all in the domain of <m>f</m>, they are critical numbers. We can also see that <m>f'</m> is never 0, so we don't have any of those types of critical numbers.
                </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \dfrac{x^2+1}{x-3}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = \frac{2x(x-3) - (x^2+1)}{(x-3)^2}</mrow>
                        <mrow> \amp = \frac{x^2-6x-1}{(x-3)^2}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = \frac{x^2-6x-1}{(x-3)^2}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = x^2-6x-1</mrow>
                        <mrow>x \amp = 3\pm \sqrt{10}</mrow>
                    </md>
                    Since <m>f'(x)=0</m> when <m>x=3-\sqrt{10}</m> and <m>x=3+\sqrt{10}</m>, these are critical numbers. We can also see that <m>f'</m> doesn't exist at <m>x=3</m>, but this is not in the domain of <m>f</m> since there is a vertical asymptote there, and so this is not a critical number.
                </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = x^2 e^{-x}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = 2xe^{-x} - x^2e^{-x}</mrow>
                        <mrow> \amp = xe^{-x}(2-x)</mrow>
                    </md>
                    We can see that <m>f'</m> is 0 at <m>x=0</m> and <m>x=2</m>, and there aren't any <m>x</m>-values where <m>f'</m> doesn't exist. This means that <m>0</m> and <m>2</m> are the only critical numbers.
                </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = x^2 e^{-x}</m> on <m>[1, 10]</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    This function is the same as above, but the domain has been limited to only <m>1\leq x\leq 10</m>. The derivative doesn't exist at these new end points, and <m>0</m> is not in the domain anymore. The critical numbers are <m>1</m>, <m>2</m>, and <m>10</m>.
                </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \ln\left(x^{4}+x+1\right)</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = \frac{4x^3+1}{x^4+x+1}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = \frac{4x^3+1}{x^4+x+1}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = 4x^3+1</mrow>
                        <mrow>-1 \amp = 4x^3</mrow>
                        <mrow>x = \frac{1}{\sqrt[3]{4}} \amp </mrow>
                    </md>
                    We can note that <m>x^4+x+1\neq 0</m>, and so this derivative will never not exist. The derivative is 0 at <m>x=\frac{1}{\sqrt[3]{4}}</m>, which is the only critical number.
                </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Find the critical numbers of the function <m>f(x)</m>, graphed below. Explain each one.
            </p>
            <figure xml:id="fig-Critical">
                <caption>Graph of <m>f(x)</m>.</caption>
                <image source="./ApplicationsDerivatives/Critical.png" width="70%">
                    <shortdescription>A function that decreases until the point (-2,-1), where it turns around (like a parabola) up to an open hole at (0,1). Then it jumps to a point at (0,2), and increases until it turns around at x=1 (like a parabola). It decreases until x=3. There is a sharp corner as it increases away from the point.</shortdescription>
                </image>
            </figure>
        </statement>
        <solution>
            <p>
                It looks like there is a horizontal tangent line at <m>x=-2</m> and <m>x=1</m>, which would mean that the derivative is 0 at each of these locations. The derivative doesn't exist at <m>x=0</m> and <m>x=3</m>. Since all of these are in the domain of <m>f</m>, we can say that all of these are critical numbers of <m>f</m>.
            </p>
        </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Give an example of a function that has <m>f'(x)\gt 0</m> on <m>(-\infty, 4)</m> and <m>f'(x)\lt 0</m> on <m>(4,\infty)</m>. Show graphically where the function is increasing and decreasing. Explain how to find out the location of a local maximum or minimum for your example.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Sketch a graph of a function that increases everywhere, but has <m>f'(4)=0</m>. Explain what sign the derivative is when <m>x\neq 4</m>.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                For each of the following functions, use the first derivative to find the intervals where the function is increasing or decreasing.
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = x^2e^x</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = 2xe^x+x^2e^x</mrow>
                        <mrow> \amp = xe^x(2+x)</mrow>
                    </md>
                    The critical numbers are <m>x=-2</m> and <m>x=0</m>.
                </p>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><p><m>x</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>(-\infty, -2)</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>-2</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>(-2,0)</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>0</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>(0,\infty)</m></p></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><p><m>f'</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\oplus</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>0</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\ominus</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>0</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\oplus</m></p></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><p><m>f</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\nearrow</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\searrow</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\nearrow</m></p></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                        <cell><p></p></cell>
                        <cell><p>increasing</p></cell>
                        <cell><p></p></cell>
                        <cell><p>decreasing</p></cell>
                        <cell><p></p></cell>
                        <cell><p>increasing</p></cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = x\ln(x)-x</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = x\left(\frac{1}{x}\right) + \ln(x) - 1</mrow>
                        <mrow> \amp = \ln(x)</mrow>
                    </md>
                    The only critical number is <m>x=1</m>.
                </p>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, 1)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>1</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(1, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(1,-1)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \dfrac{1}{x^2}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = -\frac{2}{x^3}</mrow>
                    </md>
                    This derivative doesn't exist when <m>x=0</m>, but this is not a critical number, since it's not in the domain of <m>f</m>. There's a vertical asymptote there.
                </p>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, 0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\va</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\va</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \ln(x^4 + 1)</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = \frac{4x^3}{x^4+1}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = \frac{4x^3}{x^4+1}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = 4x^3</mrow>
                        <mrow>x \amp = 0</mrow>
                    </md>
                    There is a critical number at <m>x=0</m>.
                </p>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, 0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0,0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \dfrac{x-4}{x^2+1}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = \frac{(x^2+1)-2x(x-4)}{(x^2+1)^2}</mrow>
                        <mrow> \amp = \frac{1+8x-x^2}{(x^2+1)^2}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = \frac{1+8x-x^2}{(x^2+1)^2}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = 1+8x-x^2</mrow>
                        <mrow>x \amp = 4 \pm \sqrt{17}</mrow>
                    </md>
                    These are the only critical numbers, since <m>x^2+1\neq 0</m>.
                </p>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, 4-\sqrt{17})</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>4-\sqrt{17}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(4-\sqrt{17}, 4+\sqrt{17})</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>4+\sqrt{17}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(4+\sqrt{17}, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(4-\sqrt{17},-2-\frac{\sqrt{17}}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(4+\sqrt{17} , \frac{\sqrt{17}}{2} - 2\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = e^{-x^2-2x}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = (-2x-2)e^{-x^2-2x}</mrow>
                        <mrow> \amp = -2(x+1)e^{-x^2-2x}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = -2(x+1)e^{-x^2-2x}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = x+1</mrow>
                        <mrow>x \amp = -1</mrow>
                    </md>
                </p>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, -1)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>-1</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-1, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-1,e)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \dfrac{\sqrt{x}}{e^x}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = \frac{\frac{e^x}{2\sqrt{x}} - e^x\sqrt{x}}{(e^x)^2} </mrow>{
                        <mrow> \amp = \frac{1-2x}{2e^x\sqrt{x}}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = \frac{1-2x}{2e^x\sqrt{x}}</mrow>
                        <mrow>0 \amp = 1-2x</mrow>
                        <mrow>x \amp = \frac{1}{2}</mrow>
                    </md>
                    Also note that <m>f'(0)</m> doesn't exist, and is in the domain of <m>f</m>, so this is a critical number as well.
                </p>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(0, \frac{1}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{1}{2}, \infty\right)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell>DNE</cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0,0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-1,e)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \sin(x)</m> on <m>\left[0, \frac{\pi}{2}\right]</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <m>f'(x) = \cos(x)</m> on <m>\left(0,\frac{\pi}{2})</m>. Since <m>f'(x)</m> doesn't exist at <m>x=0</m> and <m>x=\frac{\pi}{2}</m>, these are both critical points.
                </p>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(0, \frac{1}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell>DNE</cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell>DNE</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0,0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{\pi}{2},1\right)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \cos^3(x)</m> on <m>(-2\pi, 2\pi)</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        <mrow>f'(x) \amp = -3\sin(x)\cos^2(x)</mrow>
                    </md>
                    To find critical points, we'll look for where <m>\sin(x)=0</m> or <m>\cos(x)=0</m> in <m>(-2\pi,\pi)</m>:
                    <md>
                        x = -\frac{3\pi}{2}, -\pi, -\frac{\pi}{2}, 0, \frac{\pi}{2}, \pi, \frac{3\pi}{2}
                    </md>
                </p>
                 <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-2\pi, -\frac{3\pi}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>-\frac{3\pi}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\frac{3\pi}{2}, -\pi\right)</m></cell>   
                        <cell><m>-\pi</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\pi, -\frac{\pi}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>-\frac{\pi}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\frac{\pi}{2}, 0\right)</m></cell>   
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(0, \frac{\pi}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\frac{\pi}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{\pi}{2}, \pi\right)</m></cell>   
                        <cell><m>\pi</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\pi, \frac{3\pi}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\frac{3\pi}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{3\pi}{2}, 2\pi\right)</m></cell>   
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                         <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\frac{3\pi}{2},0\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\pi,-1\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\frac{\pi}{2},0\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(0,1\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{\pi}{2},0\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\pi,-1\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{3\pi}{2},0\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Explain how the First Derivative Test helps us classify critical numbers as local maximums or minimums.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Find any local maximums or local minimums for each of the following functions. Note that these are the same functions that you've already worked with in Practice Problem 6.
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = x^2e^x</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <col width="16%" top="medium"/>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><p><m>x</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>(-\infty, -2)</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>-2</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>(-2,0)</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>0</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>(0,\infty)</m></p></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><p><m>f'</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\oplus</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>0</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\ominus</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>0</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\oplus</m></p></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><p><m>f</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\nearrow</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\searrow</m></p></cell>
                        <cell><p></p></cell>
                        <cell><p><m>\nearrow</m></p></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                        <cell><p></p></cell>
                        <cell><p>increasing</p></cell>
                        <cell><p>local max</p></cell>
                        <cell><p>decreasing</p></cell>
                        <cell><p>local min</p></cell>
                        <cell><p>increasing</p></cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = x\ln(x)-x</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, 1)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>1</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(1, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(1,-1)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell>local min</cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \dfrac{1}{x^2}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, 0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\va</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\va</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \ln(x^4 + 1)</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, 0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0,0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell>local min</cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \dfrac{x-4}{x^2+1}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, 4-\sqrt{17})</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>4-\sqrt{17}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(4-\sqrt{17}, 4+\sqrt{17})</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>4+\sqrt{17}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(4+\sqrt{17}, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(4-\sqrt{17},-2-\frac{\sqrt{17}}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(4+\sqrt{17} , \frac{\sqrt{17}}{2} - 2\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell>local min</cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell>local max</cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = e^{-x^2-2x}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-\infty, -1)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>-1</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-1, \infty)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-1,e)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell>local max</cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \dfrac{\sqrt{x}}{e^x}</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(0, \frac{1}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{1}{2}, \infty\right)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell>DNE</cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0,0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(-1,e)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>local min</cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell>local max</cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \sin(x)</m> on <m>\left[0, \frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2}\right]</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(0, \frac{1}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell>DNE</cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell>DNE</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0,0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{\pi}{2},1\right)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>local min</cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell>local max</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>f(x) = \cos^3(x)</m> on <m>(-2\pi, 2\pi)</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(0, \frac{1}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell>DNE</cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell>DNE</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>(0,0)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{\pi}{2},1\right)</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>local min</cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell>local max</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
                <tabular halign="center" top="medium">
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-2\pi, -\frac{3\pi}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>-\frac{3\pi}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\frac{3\pi}{2}, -\pi\right)</m></cell>   
                        <cell><m>-\pi</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\pi, -\frac{\pi}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>-\frac{\pi}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\frac{\pi}{2}, 0\right)</m></cell>   
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(0, \frac{\pi}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\frac{\pi}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{\pi}{2}, \pi\right)</m></cell>   
                        <cell><m>\pi</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\pi, \frac{3\pi}{2}\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\frac{3\pi}{2}</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{3\pi}{2}, 2\pi\right)</m></cell>   
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="minor">
                        <cell><m>f'</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                         <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\ominus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>0</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\oplus</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell><m>f</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\frac{3\pi}{2},0\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\pi,-1\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(-\frac{\pi}{2},0\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(0,1\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{\pi}{2},0\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\searrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\pi,-1\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\left(\frac{3\pi}{2},0\right)</m></cell>
                        <cell><m>\nearrow</m></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row bottom="medium">
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell>local min</cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell>local max</cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>decreasing</cell>
                       <cell>local min</cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                       <cell></cell>
                       <cell>increasing</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </solution>
        </task>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Sketch a graph of a function <m>f(x)</m> that is continuous on <m>(-\infty,\infty)</m> and has the following characteristics. Label the intervals where <m>f</m> is increasing/decreasing, and find the locations of any local maximums/minimums.
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f'(x) \gt 0</m> on <m>(-\infty,3)</m>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f'(3)</m> does not exist
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f'(x) \lt 0</m> on <m>(3,6)</m>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f'(6)=0</m>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f'(x)\lt 0</m> on <m>(6,\infty)</m>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Sketch a graph of a function <m>f(x)</m> and has the following characteristics. Label the intervals where <m>f</m> is increasing/decreasing, and find the locations of any local maximums/minimums.
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f'(x) \lt 0</m> on <m>(-\infty,3)</m>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f'(3) = 0</m>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f'(x)\gt 0</m> on <m>(3,6)</m>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f(x)</m> has a vertical asymptote at <m>x=6</m>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <m>f'(x)\lt 0</m> on <m>(6,\infty)</m>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>
</exercises>